            <ArticleTitle>Median nerve and ulnar nerve palsy caused by calcium pyrophosphate dihydrate crystal deposition disease: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1325-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jhsa.2008.04.030</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Calcium pyrophosphate dihydrate crystal deposition disease can cause extra-articular pathology including nerve compression syndrome. We report a rare case of this complication in a 79-year-old woman.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
